{
  "id": 472520937,
  "iid": 24292,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "RTPS: Fix malformed packet error in parameterized serialized data dissection",
  "description": "When dissecting PL-CDR (parameterized) serialized data, the member\nlength field is taken from the wire without bounds checking. If the\nreported length of the remaining buffer is smaller than member_length\n(e.g. a truncated or malformed packet), the subsequent\nproto_tree_add_item() call would read past the end of the tvb,\nproducing a malformed-packet expert error.\n\nAdd a sanity check before the proto_tree_add_item() call: if fewer\nbytes remain than member_length claims, add whatever bytes are still\navailable so the partial data is visible in the tree, then break out\nof the dissection loop to avoid reading past the end of the tvb.\n\nAI-Assisted: yes (GitHub Copilot)",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2026-04-09T23:52:33.267Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-04-10T19:22:28.176Z",
